Not here
--------
No credential, API key, licence key, kubeconfig or cluster is committed. Every
script takes its host and its key as arguments and authenticates nothing by
itself.

The `use-cases/debit-order-payments/` material came out of a 2026 engagement and
was then anonymised. The customer is not named anywhere in the working tree, and
no rows of their data are included. What is reproduced is the shape of the
source: table and column names, the semantic-layer plan built over them, and the
aggregate figures the answers were checked against, kept because a walkthrough
whose expected answers are invented teaches nothing. Read it as a worked example
of the modelling, not as a synthetic dataset. If any of it is closer to the
customer than it should be, say so and it comes out.

Some reference guides record observations made against insightsoftware's own
non-production environments. Cluster names, dashboard identifiers and Confluence
and Jira keys appear where they are needed as evidence; all of them sit behind
insightsoftware authentication and none of them grants access.

